# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Cannelle et Piment Express.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to project dependencies
- **Modified**: `express_api/package.json` - Added the @vercel/analytics package
- **Modified**: `express_api/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependencies

### 2. Configuration Status
The project already had Vercel Web Analytics scripts properly configured in both HTML files:
- `express_api/public/index.html` - Analytics script present at line 2713
- `express_api/public/showcase.html` - Analytics script present at line 441

Both files include:
```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script>
  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

## Implementation Details

### Framework: Express.js (Static HTML Pages)
This is an Express.js backend API that serves static HTML pages from the `public/` directory. According to the official Vercel documentation, the HTML/static site approach is the correct implementation method.

### Analytics Integration Method
- **Script Injection**: Using Vercel's native `/_vercel/insights/script.js` path
- **Global Function**: Initialized `window.va` function for potential event tracking
- **Placement**: Scripts added before closing `</body>` tag in both HTML files

### Documentation Reference
Installation followed the latest Vercel Analytics Quickstart guide:
- https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package

## Verification

### Build Status
✅ Build completed successfully: `npm run build` passed

### Server Status  
✅ Server starts correctly: Application runs on http://localhost:3000

### Tests & Linter
- No test suite configured in project
- No linter configured in project

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Analytics will automatically start tracking page views on:
   - `/` (Landing page - index.html)
   - `/showcase` (Showcase page - showcase.html)
   - All API endpoints will be tracked as well

## Files Modified
- express_api/package.json (added @vercel/analytics dependency)
- express_api/package-lock.json (lockfile update)

## Notes
- The analytics scripts were already present in the HTML files prior to this installation
- The package installation ensures the correct version is tracked and available if programmatic usage is needed in the future
- The implementation follows Vercel's best practices for static HTML pages served by Express.js
